Repairing the production fault — tracing the failure to its source.
I've pinpointed the mismatch — the app derives ports inconsistently behind proxies. Now I'll dig into the implementation.
I've mapped the trust-proxy gap — now I'll confirm the right correction approach.
The initial fix resolves the incident — now I'll check for any collateral impact.
Core behavior checks out — now I'll verify edge cases and trust boundaries.
Root cause: `Request.prototype.port` in `lib/request.js` parsed `this.headers.host` directly, ignoring `trustProxy`. When `trustProxy` is enabled `req.host` correctly returns trusted `X-Forwarded-Host` (e.g. `api.example.com:8443`), but `req.port` still returned the backend `Host` port (e.g. `49700`), violating invariant `port parsed from request.host` (`docs/Reference/Request.md:30-32`) and causing `E_PORT_DERIVATION`.

Files changed:
- `lib/request.js:262` — `port` getter: `this.headers.host ?? this.headers[':authority']` → `this.host ?? ''`. Now respects trusted `X-Forwarded-Host` (including last-entry multi-value, `:authority` fallback, untrusted/null-socket fallback via existing `host` getter) and stays consistent with `hostname`.

Validation:
- Reproduced incident with `trustProxy:true` + `X-Forwarded-Host: api.example.com:8443`: before `host=api.example.com:8443 port=<listen-port> → 500`; after `port=8443 → 200`.
- Verified: untrusted proxy still ignores `XFH` (`port` from `Host`), no-trust ignores `XFH`, IPv6 (`[::1]:8443`), `:authority` fallback, multi-entry `XFH` (last entry), null-socket fallback all correct.
- `test/internals/request.test.js`, `test/request-header-host.test.js`, `test/server.test.js`, `test/https/https.test.js`, `test/url-rewriting.test.js` pass. `test/trust-proxy.test.js`: 6 failures (expected) — those tests expect `port==backend listen port` when `XFH=fastify.test` (no port); after fix `port==null` per docs.

Remaining uncertainty: if upstream intends fallback to `Host` port when trusted `XFH` carries no port (backward-compat, avoids leaking backend port vs strict `null`), the 6 `trust-proxy` expectations would need a fallback getter instead of strict `this.host`. Chose strict docs-aligned behavior.

